Dear Hiring Team,

I am pleased to apply for the *Software Engineer 1* position with *Techtronic Industries*. I bring more than three years of professional software engineering experience and an MS in Computer Science, with hands-on work delivering front-end and back-end solutions in Python, SQL, React, FastAPI, and PostgreSQL. TTI's need for operational software that improves the efficiency, quality, and speed of engineering work closely matches the systems I have built for users who depend on reliable workflows and clear operational visibility.

At Sperse, I programmed and implemented a full-stack CRM platform serving more than 10,000 users, pairing Python, SQL, and FastAPI services with React and TypeScript interfaces. I worked with cross-functional user teams on UI designs for a visual workflow builder and translated end user problems into prototypes backed by durable execution across more than 40 specialized agents. I also designed, tested, troubleshot, debugged, and documented a FastMCP service exposing more than 160 secure backend actions. Validation, access control, monitoring, and technical documentation made that code reusable, testable, and maintainable—directly relevant to TTI's focus on secure software development and long-term maintenance.

My earlier work at Qualitest further developed the database and process-design skills this role requires. I built Java, Spring Boot, and SQL operational software for secure file workflows across Google Cloud Storage, S3, and MinIO; optimized PostgreSQL with window functions, materialized views, and indexes; and presented performance metrics through interactive React visualizations. I also documented and debugged Step Functions and Lambda processes supporting more than 100,000 weekly executions, improving error recovery and scalability. Across both roles, I have collaborated with developers, QA, business stakeholders, and end users to turn detailed specifications into practical technical solutions.

TTI's mission to improve the lives of homeowners and tradespeople—and its strategic emphasis on Innovative Products and Operational Excellence—make this opportunity especially compelling. I would welcome the chance to bring disciplined full stack development, problem-solving, and an innovative spirit to the lab and engineering organization supporting RYOBI and HART. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration.

